  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Monday)\nIssued at 220 PM MDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nStrong ridging persists across the western CONUS with upper flow \nover the CWA becoming increasingly northwesterly. Surface obs show \nthe cold front across SCentral SD, with showers near the boundary. \nThese showers will continue SE and exit the area this afternoon. \nCurrent temps are generally in the upper 80s to mid 90s. Smoke in \nthe area has hindered temps from getting as warm as expected...and \nlikewise, apparent temps. Will leave the Heat Advisory out but could \nsee it being cancelled before 03z. Temps on Tuesday through Thursday \nwill be a cool 80s each day. After a dry day on Tuesday, a wave \npushing through is expected to bring showers and isolated \nthunderstorms overnight into Wednesday morning. Most models keep QPF \non the light side, but the ECM/RRFS/NAM show some locations getting \nwell over half an inch. This will be possible with PWATs of 150-175% \nof normal. The next series of waves will approach as the upper ridge \nweakens. These slow-moving waves are expected to bring showers and \nthunderstorms to the area late Wednesday into Thursday. The latest \nrun of the GFS shows an impressive 175-200% of normal, which could \nbring localized QPF amounts of over an inch. Hot weather with +100F \ntemps could return for the weekend as the ridge sets up again across \nthe western CONUS.",
